-- title:
--   Hasse invariant intertwines the two Hecke operators at ℓ
-- statement:
--   Let $p\ge 5$ be prime, let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $N,\ell$ be nonzero naturals with $\ell$ prime, $(N:K)\neq 0$, $p\nmid N$, $\ell\nmid N$ and $\ell\neq p$. Write $F=\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,K\,N$, the $K$-subfield of $K((q))$ generated by $j(q)$ and $j(q^N)$, and $R=\mathrm{charLDegeneracyRoof}\,K\,N\,\ell$, generated by $j(q),j(q^N),j(q^\ell),j(q^{N\ell})$; both are assumed to satisfy `IsCurveOver K`, i.e. to have principal divisors, residue fields of all places finite over $K$, and $\Omega^1$ free of rank one. Let $\alpha=$ `heckeAlphaC` be the inclusion $F\hookrightarrow R$ (through which $R$ is viewed as an $F$-algebra), $\beta=$ `heckeBetaC` the $K$-algebra map $F\to R$ given by $q\mapsto q^{\ell}$, and $h_\ell=$ `heckeMultiplier` the element of $R$ with $d(\beta\bar j)=h_\ell\cdot\alpha^{*}(d\bar j)$, where $\bar j=$ `jGeomGen` is $j(q)\in F$. Let $m,m'\ge 1$ with $m+m'=(p+1)/2$, and let $h_p\in F$ have $q$-expansion $(\theta j)^{-(p-1)/2}$, $\theta$ the operator with $\theta(f)$ having $k$-th coefficient $k\,a_k$. Then for every $f\in F$,
--   $$\ell^{\,p-2m}h_p\cdot \mathrm{Tr}_\beta\bigl(\ell^{\,m-1}h_\ell^{\,m}\cdot \alpha^{*}(f\,d\bar j)\bigr)=\ell^{\,m'-1}\,\mathrm{Tr}_{R/F}\bigl(\beta(f h_p)\,h_\ell^{\,m'}\bigr)\cdot d\bar j,$$
--   where $\alpha^{*}$ is the functorial map $\Omega^1_{F/K}\to\Omega^1_{R/K}$, $\mathrm{Tr}_\beta$ the trace map $\Omega^1_{R/K}\to\Omega^1_{F/K}$ attached to $\beta$, and exponents $p-2m$, $m-1$, $m'-1$ are natural subtractions.
--
--   This is the Hecke compatibility of the Kodaira–Spencer identification $\omega=f\,d\bar j\mapsto f h_p$ in characteristic $p$: it matches the transposed weight-$2m$ correspondence on differentials of the $\ell$-degeneracy roof with the weight-$2m'$ Hecke operator on functions, up to the factor $\ell^{\,p-2m}$. It is used in the construction of the Hecke-equivariant differential and its pairing with $\theta$ in [`ModularCurve.SSHeckeV2.exists_omegaHecke_dualMap_theta_and_exit`](thm.html#ModularCurve.SSHeckeV2.exists_omegaHecke_dualMap_theta_and_exit).
